	same conclusion under its projectivity and conditional collision hypotheses
	and the two forward comparisons~\eqref{eq:pasting-1}, for a unit state and
	$\eta,\delta\geq0$. The self-consistency comparison~\eqref{eq:pasting-2}
	is not required. The local carrier is common to both players.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	\leanok
	\uses{lem:pasting-one-sided-explicit-error, lem:pasting-coarse-commutator,
		lem:pasting-measurement, lem:pasting-scalar-error, lem:pasting-defect-bound}
	Use the fixed Schmidt mirror of the second codeword family on Alice's
	register. Its coarse consistency defect is at most $2\delta$ and its fine
	defect at most $2\delta+\eta$. The distinct-family commutator comparison
	then proves the conclusion without a register-exchange assumption.
	For the universal coarse-commutator constant $C\geq1$, one may take
	$\delta_{\mathrm{pasting}}=(3C+19)(\eta^{1/4}+\delta^{1/8})$.
	On the unit square use Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-scalar-error}; outside it,
	this error is at least $1$, so Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-defect-bound} applies.
	Thus the polynomial notation here uses the additive correction documented
	in \cite{gap:qpbt_pasting-product-error}, not the refuted product contract.
\end{proof}

\begin{definition}[Adjoining fixed basis vectors]
	\label{def:pasting-product-state}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Pasting.productPaddedState}
	\leanok
	Let $\mathcal H_A=\mathbb C^{I_A}$ and $\mathcal H_B=\mathbb C^{I_B}$,
	where $I_A,I_B$ are finite, and fix $a_0\in I_A$, $b_0\in I_B$.
	For $\psi\in\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B$, define a vector on
	$(\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B)^{\otimes2}$ by
	\[
		\Psi_{(i,b),(a,j)}
		=\mathbf 1_{b=b_0}\mathbf 1_{a=a_0}\psi_{i,j}.
	\]
	This is a formalization-only common-space realization for
	Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting}.
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Preservation under adjoining basis vectors]
	\label{lem:pasting-product-state-preservation}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Pasting.productPaddedState_norm}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Pasting.stateQForm_productPaddedState}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.Pasting.consistencyDefect_productPaddedState}
	\leanok
	\uses{def:pasting-product-state, def:consistency}
	For the preceding construction, $\|\Psi\|=\|\psi\|$. For arbitrary
	operators $A$ on $\mathcal H_A$ and $B$ on $\mathcal H_B$,
	\[
		\operatorname{Re}\langle\Psi,
		 ((A\otimes\Id)\otimes(\Id\otimes B))\Psi\rangle
		=\operatorname{Re}\langle\psi,(A\otimes B)\psi\rangle.
	\]
	Consequently every averaged off-diagonal consistency defect is preserved
	by these local placements, for arbitrary operator families and any finite
	distribution. Positivity and state normalization are not required.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	\leanok
	\uses{def:pasting-product-state}
	Expand the norm and quadratic form in the standard bases. The fixed
	coordinates remove two sums. Sum the quadratic-form identity over unequal
	answers and average over the question distribution.
\end{proof}

\begin{lemma}[Pasting on independent local spaces]
	\label{lem:pasting-heterogeneous}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_pasting_error_heterogeneous}
	\leanok
	\uses{def:consistency, def:bracket, def:povm-conventions}
	There is a universal function
	$\delta_{\mathrm{pasting}}(\eta,\delta)=\poly(\eta,\delta)$ for which
	Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons} holds with independent finite
	local spaces $\mathcal H_A$ and $\mathcal H_B$. The family $A$ acts on
	$\mathcal H_A$, the families $G_1,G_2$ act on $\mathcal H_B$, and the
	unit state belongs to $\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B$. All conditional
	collision, projectivity, and forward comparison hypotheses, and the
	conclusion~\eqref{eq:pasting-3}, are retained. This is a
	formalization-only strengthening of Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting}.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	\leanok
	\uses{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons, lem:pasting-product-state-preservation,
		lem:pasting-tensor-placement}
	A unit state implies that both local spaces are nonzero. Choose one basis
	vector in each and adjoin them as in Definition~\ref{def:pasting-product-state}.
	The common local space is $\mathcal H_A\otimes\mathcal H_B$.
	Tensor placement preserves projectivity, postprocessing, and the product
	$G_2G_1G_2$. Both input defects and the pasted output defect are unchanged.
	Apply Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting-forward-comparisons} on this common space.
\end{proof}

\begin{lemma}[Universal bound for placed consistency defects]
	\label{lem:pasting-defect-bound}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.consistencyDefect_placed_le_one}
	\leanok
	\uses{def:consistency, def:povm-conventions}
	Let $\mu$ be a probability law on a finite question set, let $A^x_a$ and
	$B^x_a$ be measurements on the two tensor factors with the same finite
	outcome set, and let $\psi$ be a unit vector. Then
	\[
		\E_{x\sim\mu}\sum_{a\ne b}
		\langle\psi|A^x_a\ot B^x_b|\psi\rangle\leq1.
	\]
	This is formalization support for the complementary error regime of
	Lemma~\ref{lem:pasting}; projectivity is not required.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
	\leanok
	Completeness makes the sum over all outcome pairs equal to $1$.
	Removing the nonnegative diagonal terms can only decrease it.
\end{proof}

\begin{lemma}[Scalar comparison for the pasting error]
	\label{lem:pasting-scalar-error}
	\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.pasting_error_sqrt_le_rpow}
	\leanok
	For $C\geq1$ and $0\leq\eta,\delta\leq1$, set
	\[
		K=C\delta+(2\sqrt{2\delta}+2\delta+2\sqrt{C\delta}+C\delta)
		  +2\eta+2\sqrt{2(\delta+2\sqrt{2\delta}+\eta)}
		  +2\sqrt{2(\delta+2\sqrt{2\delta})}.
	\]

